 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates `input` against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before calling
+  the executor (`required`, declared property types and `enum`; unknown extra properties still pass
+  through unchanged, and types are neither coerced nor defaulted). A static tool's schema is compiled
+  once at `register` time so a broken schema fails at startup; a function-valued tool definition has its
+  schema compiled and cached per returned schema object. When validation fails, `execute` returns a
+  `ToolResponse` naming the failing property paths and constraints without echoing or logging the
+  offending values, so the orchestrator sends the rejection back to the model as a `tool_result` within
+  `maxToolRounds` instead of aborting the turn. **Migration:** an executor that used to hand-validate its
+  input now receives only input the schema already accepts, and a tool that relied on seeing malformed
+  input to produce its own error message stops seeing it.
+
